## Querying Local Database

Use Supabase Studio SQL editor (easiest):
http://localhost:54323

Or via CLI:
```bash
npx supabase db query "SELECT * FROM your_table LIMIT 10;"
```

Or via REST:
```bash
curl 'http://localhost:54321/rest/v1/your_table?select=*&limit=10' \
  --header 'apikey: $VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY' \
  --header 'Authorization: Bearer $VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY'
```
## Deploying Edge Functions to Production

Deploy a single function:
```bash
npx supabase functions deploy 
```

Deploy all functions:
```bash
npx supabase functions deploy
```

Deploy with env vars (if not already set in Supabase dashboard):
```bash
npx supabase functions deploy  --env-file supabase/functions/.env
```

## Local vs Production

- Local dev: `npx supabase functions serve` — hot-reloads on file save, no deploy needed
- Production: must explicitly run `npx supabase functions deploy <function-name>` after changes
- New functions: create folder + index.ts at `supabase/functions/<function-name>/index.ts`, then deploy please always ask me before doing this

## Creating a New Edge Function

```bash
# Scaffold a new function
npx supabase functions new 

# Then edit: supabase/functions//index.ts
# Test locally via functions serve, then deploy when ready
npx supabase functions deploy 
```